<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/storm-sky.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/storm-sky-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/storm-sky.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal-services/">Services</a></li><li aria-current="page">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Windstorm and Tornado Damage Appraisal in Washington</h1><p class="lede">Washington’s worst weather often arrives as wind. From the 1962 Columbus Day Storm to the November 2024 bomb cyclone, big Pacific lows have left long trails of roof, siding and fence claims.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-y" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Peak season</dt><dd>October–March</dd></div><div><dt>Big events</dt><dd>1962, 2006, 2015, 2024</dd></div><div><dt>Also seen</dt><dd>Brief tornadoes</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>A wind state more than a storm state</h2>
<p>Powerful Pacific lows reach Washington most winters. Some are historic: the Columbus Day Storm of October 1962, the Inauguration Day Storm of January 1993, the Hanukkah Eve Storm of December 2006 and the bomb cyclone of November 19, 2024, which cut power to hundreds of thousands of Puget Sound homes. East of the mountains, the November 2015 windstorm brought down trees and power lines across Spokane.</p>
<p>Tornadoes are rare but not unknown. A 1972 tornado damaged parts of Vancouver, and an EF-2 tornado struck Port Orchard in December 2018. Brief tornadoes and downbursts can also cause damage in eastern Washington during summer storms.</p>
<h2>How wind claims go wrong</h2>
<ul>
<li>Lifted shingles that resealed and are approved as a handful of repairs instead of a slope replacement.</li>
<li>Siding replaced only on the damaged wall, leaving obvious mismatches on a continuous elevation.</li>
<li>Fences, sheds and carports valued at a token amount without measured lengths or materials.</li>
<li>Interior water damage from wind-driven rain treated as a separate, excluded leak.</li>
<li>Debris removal, tree removal and temporary protection under-documented.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Evidence that holds up</h2>
<p>Wind damage is directional. We photograph each elevation, note which slopes faced the wind, and record crease lines, missing tabs and broken seal strips. We tie that to the storm on your date of loss using public weather records. When a fallen tree is part of the claim, see our <a href="/insurance-appraisal-services/tree-impact-claim-appraisal/">tree impact appraisal</a> page.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Deductibles</b>Washington policies usually apply a standard flat deductible to wind losses rather than a hurricane-style percentage, but some carriers use separate wind or hail deductibles. Check your declarations page.</div>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How do I prove when the wind damage happened?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Dated photos, neighbor claims, utility outage records and National Weather Service storm reports all help tie damage to a specific event.</p></div></details><details><summary>My power was out for days and food spoiled. Is that covered?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Some policies offer limited coverage for food spoilage after a power outage, often as an endorsement. Check your policy and declarations page.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can wind damage be found months later?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Creased shingles and broken seals are easy to miss. Report it as soon as you find it and keep a record of when and how you discovered it.</p></div></details></div><h2>Related services</h2><div class="cards3 tight"><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/tree-impact-claim-appraisal/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/fallen-tree-house.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/fallen-tree-house-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/fallen-tree-house.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Fallen Tree Damage Appraisal</h3><span class="pcard-p">Douglas fir, cedar and maple impacts on roofs, framing and decks, plus removal and crane costs.</span><span class="pcard-more">Learn more <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/water-rain-intrusion-appraisal/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/water-damage.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/water-damage-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/water-damage.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Water &amp; Rain Intrusion Appraisal</h3><span class="pcard-p">Burst pipes, supply-line failures and wind-driven rain, valued with moisture mapping and full drying scopes.</span><span class="pcard-more">Learn more <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/house-fire-smoke-appraisal/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/house-fire.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/house-fire-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/house-fire.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</h3><span class="pcard-p">Structure fires, smoke and soot cleaning, odor control and contents losses priced room by